{"t": 784.24, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 2, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "Dual-Ended-Boost", "rationale": "The open-circuit voltage of the piezo is very low (0.76V), and previous bridge-rectifier designs suffered from excessive diode drops (0.5V) and inefficient boosting. This topology uses two independent boost paths, one for each half-cycle. Each path uses a dedicated inductor and switch to elevate the voltage. To complete the current loop during both the charging and discharging phases of the inductors, two return diodes are used to connect the piezo terminals to ground. This eliminates the double-diode drop of a full-bridge and provides a higher voltage gain, ensuring the 1.8V output threshold is reached even under weak excitation.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "Dual-Ended-Boost", "rationale": "The open-circuit voltage of the piezo is very low (0.76V), and previous bridge-rectifier designs suffered from excessive diode drops (0.5V) and inefficient boosting. This topology uses two independent boost paths, one for each half-cycle. Each path uses a dedicated inductor and switch to elevate the voltage. To complete the current loop during both the charging and discharging phases of the inductors, two return diodes are used to connect the piezo terminals to ground. This eliminates the double-diode drop of a full-bridge and provides a higher voltage gain, ensuring the 1.8V output threshold is reached even under weak excitation.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.001}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "0"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n1", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 0.0001, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "pos"}, {"id": "L2", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzn", "n2"], "value": 0.001}, {"id": "S2", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n2", "0"], "ctrl": "G2"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "G2", "t