{"t": 1034.33, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 3, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "Single-Sync-Boost", "rationale": "Previous designs failed either due to high power consumption of multiple SYNC controllers on weak excitation (S4) or inability to cold start. This design implements a dual-inductor boost converter controlled by a single SYNC to minimize overhead (0.5 uA). Two inductors L1 and L2 extract energy from both half-cycles of the piezo current, pushing charge to the storage capacitor via D1 and D2. This topology is structurally a SECE-like converter and is expected to provide the necessary voltage boost to reach 1.8 V from the low open-circuit voltage (0.76 V) of the piezo transducer.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "Single-Sync-Boost", "rationale": "Previous designs failed either due to high power consumption of multiple SYNC controllers on weak excitation (S4) or inability to cold start. This design implements a dual-inductor boost converter controlled by a single SYNC to minimize overhead (0.5 uA). Two inductors L1 and L2 extract energy from both half-cycles of the piezo current, pushing charge to the storage capacitor via D1 and D2. This topology is structurally a SECE-like converter and is expected to provide the necessary voltage boost to reach 1.8 V from the low open-circuit voltage (0.76 V) of the piezo transducer.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.002}, {"id": "L2", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzn", "n2"], "value": 0.002}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "0"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "S2", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n2", "0"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n1", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 5e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 2.2e-06}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "mod