{"t": 1297.83, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 4, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "Balanced-Boost", "rationale": "The previous designs failed because the piezo's open-circuit voltage (0.76V) is too low to power a 1.8V load, and simple SSHI only doubles this voltage (to 1.52V), which is still insufficient. I am proposing a Balanced Boost topology that uses the full differential voltage between pzp and pzn as the source for two boost paths. By connecting the inductors across the piezo terminals during the switching phase, we capture energy from both half-cycles and boost it to the output. This topology maximizes the available voltage swing and uses a single SYNC to drive both paths, improving efficiency and cold-start potential.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "Balanced-Boost", "rationale": "The previous designs failed because the piezo's open-circuit voltage (0.76V) is too low to power a 1.8V load, and simple SSHI only doubles this voltage (to 1.52V), which is still insufficient. I am proposing a Balanced Boost topology that uses the full differential voltage between pzp and pzn as the source for two boost paths. By connecting the inductors across the piezo terminals during the switching phase, we capture energy from both half-cycles and boost it to the output. This topology maximizes the available voltage swing and uses a single SYNC to drive both paths, improving efficiency and cold-start potential.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.001}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n1", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "L2", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzn", "n2"], "value": 0.001}, {"id": "S2", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n2", "pzp"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["n2", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"