{"t": 1976.54, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 7, "k": 1, "move": "modify_topology", "name": "Pure-SSHI", "rationale": "The previous P-SSHI failed because the full-bridge rectifier (specifically the bottom diodes D3 and D4) clamped the piezo voltage to -0.25V. This prevents the voltage across the piezo capacitor Cp from building up and flipping to a large negative value, which is the core mechanism of the SSHI (Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor) technique. By removing the bottom diodes and keeping only the output harvesting diodes (D1, D2), the piezo voltage can swing freely, allowing the inductor to effectively 'flip' the charge and boost the voltage above the output threshold (1.8V).", "circuit": {"move": "modify_topology", "name": "Pure-SSHI", "rationale": "The previous P-SSHI failed because the full-bridge rectifier (specifically the bottom diodes D3 and D4) clamped the piezo voltage to -0.25V. This prevents the voltage across the piezo capacitor Cp from building up and flipping to a large negative value, which is the core mechanism of the SSHI (Synchronized Switch Harvesting on Inductor) technique. By removing the bottom diodes and keeping only the output harvesting diodes (D1, D2), the piezo voltage can swing freely, allowing the inductor to effectively 'flip' the charge and boost the voltage above the output threshold (1.8V).", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.001}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 1.5e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 2.2e-06}, {"id": "DZ1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}]}}
